          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Nature of the connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.2fr;"><span>IPSAS 1</span><span>Material item disclosure at the entity level – para. 56 encourages evaluating significance at the SEGMENT level too (§8)</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.2fr;"><span>IPSAS 2</span><span>Segment cash flow disclosure encouragement follows IPSAS 2's operating/investing/financing framework (§8)</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.2fr;"><span>IPSAS 3</span><span>Governs restatement mechanics for segment accounting policy changes (§7)</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.2fr;"><span>IPSAS 12</span><span>Cost allocation guidance usable for attributing costs to segments (§6)</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.2fr;"><span>IPSAS 22</span><span>General Government Sector disclosure – a distinct statistical-basis alternative, not a segment-reporting substitute (§4)</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.2fr;"><span>IPSAS 35</span><span>Intra-economic-entity eliminations occur BEFORE segment revenue/expense/assets/liabilities are determined (§6)</span></div>
